{"name":"Cabin Plank","hex":"#574038","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small dwelling characteristic of the frontier, especially when built from logs with simple tools and not constructed by professional builders, but by those who meant to live in it.","A chalet or lodge, especially one that can hold large groups of people."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a cabin or other small space.","To limit the scope of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin"},{"term":"plank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, broad and thick piece of timber, as opposed to a board which is less thick.\nA flat piece of wood on which to cook fish, so that the wood provides flavor and helps to produce a pleasing texture.","A flat piece of wood on which to cook fish, so that the wood provides flavor and helps to produce a pleasing texture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover something with planking.","To bake (fish, etc.) on a piece of cedar lumber."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plank"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plank (wood)","blocks":[{"text":"A plank is timber that is flat, elongated, and rectangular with parallel faces that are higher and longer than wide. Used primarily in carpentry, planks are critical in the construction of ships, houses, bridges, and many other structures. Planks also serve as supports to form shelves and tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/US_Navy_090513-N-1060K-122_Ship_restorers_Chris_Hanlon%2C_bottom%2C_and_Paul_Chiasson_line_up_a_new_plank_of_white_oak_along_USS_Constitution%27s_starboard_side.jpg/330px-US_Navy_090513-N-1060K-122_Ship_restorers_Chris_Hanlon%2C_bottom%2C_and_Paul_Chiasson_line_up_a_new_plank_of_white_oak_along_USS_Constitution%27s_starboard_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plank_(w